Package: litearm-can-dkms
Version: @VERSION@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: LiteArm Team <support@litearm.com>
Depends: dkms, build-essential
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-realtime
Replaces: litearm-vr-bridge
Description: LiteArm CAN: gs_usb driver that fits the STM32 arm board, auto bring-up
 DKMS build of gs_usb for the LiteArm STM32 composite board (arm CDC + CAN).
 Reads the bulk endpoints from the interface descriptor (firmware versions
 differ) and repairs an inconsistent bit-timing range, so can0 carries frames on
 any firmware.  Also installs a udev rule that brings CAN interfaces up at 1 Mbit/s
 and a self-test (litearm-can-selftest) that detects a "UP but silent" interface.
